<rule>
  <description>GitHub Remote and Live URL for the Personal Portfolio</description>
  <instructions>
    - The live URL for this personal website/portfolio is https://apisit-man.github.io.
    - When performing Git operations (such as pushing code), always ensure the target repository is `apisit-man/apisit-man.github.io`.
    - Do NOT use or reference the old repository `apisittongchai/apisittongchai.github.io`.
  </instructions>
</rule>

<rule>
  <description>Strict Personal Branding & Institutional Independence with Factual Citation Whitelist</description>
  <instructions>
    - This repository (apisit-man.github.io) is Dr. Apisit Tongchai's strictly PERSONAL website, portfolio, and independent research lab.
    - WHAT IS PROHIBITED (Institutional Affiliation / Endorsement):
      * NEVER represent the website, newly authored tools, simulations, games, or independent research as official outputs or endorsed works of "สสวท.", "IPST", or any employer.
      * NEVER assign institutional titles (e.g., "ผู้เชี่ยวชาญ สสวท.", "IPST Specialist") in author bylines, bio badges, site headers, footers, or Schema.org author metadata. Always use approved independent titles like "ดร.อภิสิทธิ์ ธงไชย", "นักวิจัยและนักการศึกษา", "Independent Educator & Researcher".
    - PROTECTED WHITELIST (MANDATORY FACTUAL & CITATION INTEGRITY):
      * DO NOT modify, censor, or rename published academic journal/magazine titles or historical citations (e.g., "นิตยสาร สสวท.", "IPST Magazine" are factual publication venues and must remain exact).
      * DO NOT remove or replace valid organizational contact addresses (e.g., atong@ipst.ac.th), CV educational/career history, or external reading links (e.g., emagazine.ipst.ac.th) unless explicitly requested by the user.
      * When performing audits, bug checks, or refactorings, NEVER flag or change historical bibliographic citations or contact channels as branding violations.
  </instructions>
</rule>

<rule>
  <description>Continuous Skill Self-Improvement & Global/Cloud Synchronization</description>
  <instructions>
    - Whenever the user provides feedback, corrections, design preferences, troubleshooting lessons, or new workflow instructions during a task that uses (or relates to) an installed skill, you MUST proactively update and improve that skill's `SKILL.md` (and any relevant files in `references/` or `scripts/`) so the agent permanently learns from the user's comments.
    - Whenever a skill is created or improved, ALWAYS synchronize it across BOTH locations on this PC:
      1. Workspace Cloud Directory: `c:\Users\atong\Documents\antigravity\personal website\.agents\skills\<skill-name>\`
      2. Global PC Directory: `C:\Users\atong\.gemini\config\skills\<skill-name>\`
      (You can run `.\.agents\sync-skills.ps1 -Mode Both` to keep both directories 100% in sync.)
    - When pushing changes or wrapping up skill improvements in the workspace, stage and push `.agents/` to `origin` (`apisit-man/apisit-man.github.io`) so the cloud repository always has the latest evolved skills.
  </instructions>
</rule>
